          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Industry context</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Public infrastructure demands sovereign-grade networks</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Smart city initiatives across the our region require deep fibre connectivity reaching municipal facilities, transport corridors and public safety zones. Government entities need networks that are sovereign, auditable and resilient to disruption, with IoT sensor grids feeding real-time data into centralised command centres. Abu Dhabi's sovereign cloud partnership with Microsoft and Core42 (G42) — processing over 11 million daily digital interactions — exemplifies the region's ambition for AI-native government by 2027.</p>
          <p>Cybersecurity is a non-negotiable requirement for public-sector infrastructure. National cybersecurity frameworks mandate data residency, segmented access and continuous monitoring. Saudi Arabia and the UAE are leading sovereign AI platform investments exceeding $100 billion, creating demand for sovereign cloud and compute infrastructure that keeps government data within national borders. MEAICON designs infrastructure that meets these obligations while keeping smart city services running around the clock.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

